      "id": "claim_f1110125ebd74ebeaa4192b82a7130de",
      "statement": "The coding agent assembles middleware outer to inner beginning with filesystem and conversation offloading, then preparation/transcript/tool layers and tool guards, followed by queue/reply hooks, model selection/fallback and dynamic tools, and ending with message sanitization, stable result ordering, model error recording, and the innermost model-call timeout; several entries are conditional on run mode or configured capabilities.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/server.py#L1978-L2111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fae640cac83952ac5ff2dd3342609197265c34b1671436c5cb735992c5ac8579:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bc2694952fef40c7b38a652aaff8f126",
      "statement": "The reviewer uses a distinct smaller chain: preparation, call limit, tool error handling, proxy refresh and message queue, provider sanitizers, orphaned-call repair, stable ordering, timeout retry, model error recording, model deadline, and review-check settlement. It therefore does not inherit the coding agent's model fallback, selection, tool guards, or transcript/offloading assembly.",
